WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.579 --> 00:00:03.686
(audience cheering)
Doctor love!

00:00:03.686 --> 00:00:05.560
(man in audience hollering)

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.950
I actually wish that you would come out

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.170
to the West Wing theme.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.750
I think that would have been hilarious.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:10.583
All right, try it again.
Can we have him see,

00:00:10.583 --> 00:00:11.710
can we see, I wanna see
Gene Simmons come out

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:12.950
to the West Wing theme.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.450
Let's see that again, a
more stately Gene Simmons.

00:00:16.458 --> 00:00:19.291
("The West Wing")

00:00:21.356 --> 00:00:24.523
(audience applauding)

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.530
So much to talk about.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.610
Yeah, so little time.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:34.443
So little time.

00:00:34.443 --> 00:00:35.560
That's a nice-looking book.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.874
Isn't it nice?
Wow.

00:00:37.874 --> 00:00:38.950
(audience laughing)

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.060
New York Times bestseller, I hear.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:44.240
You whore. (laughs)
(audience laughing)

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.270
That's all I can say.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.730
We'll get to the book in a minute,

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.440
but first let's give the
people what they want,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.263
the famous Gene Simmons tongue.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.248
Yeah!
No, no, no, no.

00:00:52.248 --> 00:00:54.044
You gotta--
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:00:54.044 --> 00:00:56.847
(audience cheering)
Gene!

00:00:56.847 --> 00:00:58.113
You ready?
Yeah!

00:01:00.077 --> 00:01:02.932
(audience laughing)

00:01:02.932 --> 00:01:07.932
Whoa.
(audience whooping)

00:01:08.176 --> 00:01:11.759
(Conan groaning in horror)

00:01:13.923 --> 00:01:16.923
(audience cheering)

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:26.789
You just ruined the
West Wing theme forever.

00:01:26.789 --> 00:01:27.630
(audience laughing)

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:28.463
Hi, Max.
(Conan laughing)

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:31.740
You know, honestly, no
joke, that's a great band.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.564
That's the greatest band in late night.

00:01:33.564 --> 00:01:35.257
(audience cheering)

00:01:35.257 --> 00:01:37.674
Thank you, Gene, thank you.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:41.540
Let me, because we have limited time

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:44.480
and there's so much to talk
about, let me ask you quickly.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.440
First of all, you wore the makeup.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.530
Then there was a period in the 80s

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:49.740
when you didn't wear the makeup.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.010
Right.
Then you started

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.330
wearing the makeup again.
Right.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:53.940
Was there ever a transitional period

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.213
where you wore half makeup?

00:01:55.213 --> 00:01:57.230
(audience laughing)
Did that, never happened?

00:01:57.230 --> 00:01:58.063
You never thought of it?

00:01:58.063 --> 00:01:59.000
Would you ever think about that?

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.940
Pay me.
Okay, I'll pay you.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.540
Do your kids understand?

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:03.373
(audience laughing)

00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:05.070
Do you have, I have so
many questions to get to.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.255
Do your children, you
have kids, do they know--

00:02:07.255 --> 00:02:08.510
I have two that I know of, yeah.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.440
Oh.
(audience laughing)

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.307
What a wonderful line for the ladies.

00:02:12.307 --> 00:02:13.690
(audience laughing)
Well I mean it's true.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.070
I mean--
You have two kids, you said.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.580
Do your kids know what you do?

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:17.460
Do they--
Oh yeah.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:20.410
My boy is now 13 years old.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:23.130
My daughter's about nine, going on 10.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.377
And of course on the day in
school, when everybody said,

00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:26.920
"What does your mom and
dad do for a living?"

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.960
and so on and so forth, they
came in as little dentists

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.437
and little hairdressers and so on.

00:02:30.437 --> 00:02:32.580
And my kid came in with a six-foot poster,

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.830
which he sort of unrolled,

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:35.870
and there I am drooling
blood and spitting fire,

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:38.108
and he said, "That's my dad."

00:02:38.108 --> 00:02:39.030
(audience laughing)

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:39.863
Well, I bet he's proud, though.

00:02:39.863 --> 00:02:42.880
Oh yeah, we've got KISS comic
books, KISS cell phones,

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:43.713
KISS everything, you know.

00:02:43.713 --> 00:02:45.470
Like all the cool stuff the kids have.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.330
So if you're gonna go home,

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:48.980
never leave home without it, babe.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.720
Well now can we see--
Because the KISS Visa card

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.423
is right there, you can have it.

00:02:52.423 --> 00:02:53.820
(audience groaning)
Yeah, hey, God,

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:54.864
I'm looking good, too.

00:02:54.864 --> 00:02:55.880
Look at that.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.120
Is there nothing you won't do?

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.220
(audience laughing)

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.130
You've really got KISS cell phone?

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:02.070
Oh yeah.
Is it like any other

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.220
cell phone, but it just has

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.814
the little members of the band on it?

00:03:04.814 --> 00:03:06.141
Well, the difference is you have to buy it

00:03:06.141 --> 00:03:07.625
and then I get paid.

00:03:07.625 --> 00:03:10.330
(audience laughing)

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.200
Nice pitch you've got
there for the product.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.830
It's true, I think you've got something--

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.295
That makes me want to have one.

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:16.128
(Gene laughing)

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.270
You brought something backstage

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.650
which I find hard to believe.

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:19.940
I understand it's backstage right now,

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:20.940
we're gonna wheel this out?

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.240
Good idea.
All right, let's take a,

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.257
this is actually for
sale, it's a KISS coffin.

00:03:25.257 --> 00:03:28.340
(audience chuckling)

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.650
You gotta see the top, it's really cool.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:33.560
Can we see the back?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.410
Oh no, the back's the same as the front.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:39.260
By the way, this is
available at kisssonline.com,

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.978
or at your local funeral house.

00:03:42.978 --> 00:03:43.811
(audience chuckling)

00:03:43.811 --> 00:03:45.880
And by the way, if you're
watching, this is a real one.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.270
And if you're watching the ball game,

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:50.330
you don't have to wait to die
for me to get a buck, really.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.960
You can actually reach in
there and grab a cold one,

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.908
'cause it's actually a cooler.

00:03:54.908 --> 00:03:59.908
(audience chuckling)
(audience applauding)

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:06.971
You know, by the way,
tomorrow, even as we sit here--

00:04:06.971 --> 00:04:08.560
(audience laughing)

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:12.560
What made you decide that the
world needed a KISS coffin?

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.380
I mean, what made you think,
"I've got it, KISS coffin."

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.260
Are there people that want
a KISS coffin, seriously?

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:18.540
Yeah it's actually, seriously--

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.924
Has anyone bought, has one been sold?

00:04:19.924 --> 00:04:21.910
Tons, thousands.
Not true.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:23.076
Sports--
You lie.

00:04:23.076 --> 00:04:23.996
(audience laughing)

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:25.340
You know what? You know what?

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:28.470
Get online, there's White
Light Casket Company,

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:29.820
they produce it for us.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:30.760
Sports bars, concert halls--

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.098
I know it's being sold,
but has anyone bought one?

00:04:33.098 --> 00:04:34.260
Has there been one--
Oh yeah, tons.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.870
Literally, they're in sports bars.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:36.970
You know, guys want to drink, you know,

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:38.441
they're watching the
ball game and everything,

00:04:38.441 --> 00:04:39.274
and all of a sudden--
Oh, as a cooler, but there's

00:04:39.274 --> 00:04:40.514
no one who wants to go--
Well that's what I said

00:04:40.514 --> 00:04:41.347
over there.
Into to the hereafter right,

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:42.490
but no one really wants
to go into the hereafter

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.260
in a KISS coffin.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.421
Why not?
(audience laughing)

00:04:46.421 --> 00:04:48.480
(Conan laughing)

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.172
It's that logic, you...

00:04:50.172 --> 00:04:51.646
(audience applauding)

00:04:51.646 --> 00:04:53.810
I can't argue with that logic, why not.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:57.180
All right, this blew my mind.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:00.410
This is really available,
you're selling these.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.280
People, look at this,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.483
It's a KISS checkbook right here.

00:05:03.483 --> 00:05:05.933
[Gene] Now that's what
I'm talking about, yeah.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.013
By the way, just make it out--

00:05:08.013 --> 00:05:11.100
It's just if I wrote someone
a check on a KISS checkbook,

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.130
and tried to buy something
like over a thousand dollars,

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:15.220
don't you think I'd get some,

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:16.360
but wouldn't I be in danger

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:17.610
that people think it would be a gag?

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.530
It's like that money
that has the moose on it,

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:20.990
President Moose, you know?

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:21.823
No, no, no, no.

00:05:21.823 --> 00:05:24.710
This is currency recognized
around the world.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:27.900
If it says KISS on it,
don't worry, It's legit.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.267
By the way, just make it out
to Gene Simmons, you know.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:31.406
(audience laughing)

00:05:31.406 --> 00:05:34.961
(Conan yelps)
(audience cheering)

00:05:34.961 --> 00:05:37.215
(Conan laughing)

00:05:37.215 --> 00:05:38.721
Oh, but I have to say,
(Conan laughing)

00:05:38.721 --> 00:05:39.554
I gotta say one thing--

00:05:39.554 --> 00:05:40.387
It's like working with an animal.

00:05:40.387 --> 00:05:43.346
Don't get too close. (gobbles comically)

00:05:43.346 --> 00:05:45.750
I have to thank everybody,
you know, from my heart.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.820
I was born in Israel,
which you'll find out

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.384
when you buy "Kiss and Makeup".

00:05:49.384 --> 00:05:50.270
(audience laughing)

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.700
I'm gonna be at the Virgin
Megastore tomorrow at 6:00 p.m.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.940
in Times Square, come and see me.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.140
But the most important
thing is thank you all.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:59.100
Thank you so much for
making KISS the number one

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.220
American group gold record
winners of all time.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.010
Our box set just went gold.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.850
We're now beat every other American band.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.765
Thank you so much, I love you.

00:06:07.765 --> 00:06:11.570
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:15.830
Well, I thank you for being here, Gene.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.570
There's two things at the
bottom I'm supposed to plug,

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:19.452
but you just did that for me.

00:06:19.452 --> 00:06:20.285
(audience laughing)
I did.

00:06:20.285 --> 00:06:22.462
I actually think you did it
12 times during the segment.

00:06:22.462 --> 00:06:23.700
(audience laughing)

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:26.895
All right, that's our
infomercial for the evening.

00:06:26.895 --> 00:06:27.728
(audience chuckling)

00:06:27.728 --> 00:06:28.764
Gene Simmons, everybody,
we'll take a break,

00:06:28.764 --> 00:06:30.181
we'll be right--

